<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idbad38e48a55d6518ef82b32a4d96fee65264aae" commit="e18f8446102206c107aad1091cc06033c4ffdc75" commit_message="usb_pd_protocol: Rename PD_FLAGS_DATA_SWAPPED to _CHECK_IDENTITY  Rename the variable to actually tell us what it does (it sends a Discover Identity command), instead of littering the code with comments explaining why we set DATA_SWAPPED when the data roles have not really been swapped.  BRANCH=none BUG=chromium:644663 TEST=make buildall -j  Change-Id: Idbad38e48a55d6518ef82b32a4d96fee65264aae Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/415696 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="415696" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/96/415696/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I55b6658c2bc0574b8427ae086f61daf03730a725" commit="a3fa4a706a982c064e8674d3eaf2d5d5a8d97c64" commit_message="usb_pd_policy: Automatically swap vconn if adapter requests it  During discovery, if adapter requests vconn power in the AMA flags, make sure that we provide vconn.  This, for example, is necessary for the Apple HDMI adapter to work on boot, when connected in S5. In that case, adapter does request vconn swap, but we reject that as the system is off, and, therefore 5V supply is off. On boot, we send another discovery request, which will detect this case and swap the power.  BRANCH=none BUG=chromium:644663 TEST=On elm, S5. Plug adapter with power+HDMI. Switch on elm,      type &quot;pd 0 vdm ident&quot; in console, display works.  Change-Id: I55b6658c2bc0574b8427ae086f61daf03730a725 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/415697 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="415697" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/97/415697/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I21d47c69e2c7153a5d808dedcb1abe360ce3f5c0" commit="194541df3535982e4db80db49cab2a8d908cc0f0" commit_message="usb_pd_protocol: Force rediscovering identity on boot  This is useful with Apple's HDMI adapter, as the code that sends the discovery message will also swap vconn as required.  BRANCH=none BUG=chromium:644663 TEST=On elm, S5. Plug adapter with power+HDMI. Switch on elm,      display works.  Change-Id: I21d47c69e2c7153a5d808dedcb1abe360ce3f5c0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/415698 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="415698" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/98/415698/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7ef61140081ec2e466fc8eace854ec02c065c6da" commit="ecc9d7b488150a66f010d6d0890749aa02432f04" commit_message="CRAS: client - Fix Chrome crash when input buffer overrun  When an input client hangs at processing the captured buffer, server side could encounter buffer overrun. When that happens and client later recovers from busy state, the read buffer would no longer be a whole captured chunk. Assuming Chrome processes the read buffer while it's in the middle of overrun, only partial of the buffer is consumed and that causes non-zero read offset. This makes Chrome crash at the next time it handles capture data because buffer pointer won't start from the beginning.  BUG=chromium:673454 TEST=Run apprtc app on Kevin.  Change-Id: I7ef61140081ec2e466fc8eace854ec02c065c6da Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/418130 Commit-Ready: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="418130" owner_email="hychao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/30/418130/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic9eab3da91c25709a0ccf9df5b8c9168529260ca" commit="e7a5198f35312309132662d789208a76f62b3a00" commit_message="CRAS: dev_stream - Remove unused variable  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: Ic9eab3da91c25709a0ccf9df5b8c9168529260ca Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/418131 Commit-Ready: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="418131" owner_email="hychao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/31/418131/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If50eb3dace5e2b5001928a03489e5fbb961af869" commit="19e1fae0ebaf5b7368ea757d16167d50708c351a" commit_message="telemetry_Benchmarks: Add page_cycler_v2.typical_25  BUG=chromium:674016 TEST=test_that --args local=True DUT_IP telemetry_Benchmarks.page_cycler_v2.typical_25  Change-Id: If50eb3dace5e2b5001928a03489e5fbb961af869 Signed-off-by: Chung-yih Wang &lt;cywang@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/419939 Reviewed-by: Ben Cheng &lt;bccheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="419939" owner_email="cywang@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/39/419939/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifd4cd9912ab505427c985154b3f469e1485789b2" commit="4d76615b6d2be13cc1ecaa68b126aceba042e27d" commit_message="scripts: Change anti-rollback check from error to warning for make_dev_firmware.  Currently make_dev_firmware will abort if the stored TPM version is higher and ask user to reset TPM; however that is not very feasible because:  (1) If the device is still MP-signed, external users can't boot     dev-signed factory shim or recovery or test images. (2) Even if the user is able to reset TPM, the stored TPM version     will be increased again when user boots into the image for     running make_dev_firmware.  As a result, the right flow is to allow user (with warning and instructions) resign firmware with dev-keys, boot into recovery mode due to anti-rollback check, and then boot any dev-signed image to reset TPM.  BRANCH=none BUG=None TEST=./make_dev_firmware.sh # see warning message.  Change-Id: Ifd4cd9912ab505427c985154b3f469e1485789b2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/419898 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="419898" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/98/419898/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie002e5807d1e616da034dbb8896867572e148e00" commit="87cd72488f2cd2f975994a7480db3c617f3ce72b" commit_message="CR50: fix errors flagged by coverity  - Update SHA_DIGEST_MAX_BYTES to reflect SHA-512 support - Fix unitialized variable error in tpm2/hash.c  BRANCH=none BUG=none CQ-DEPEND=CL:419327 TEST=make buildall succeeds  Change-Id: Ie002e5807d1e616da034dbb8896867572e148e00 Signed-off-by: nagendra modadugu &lt;ngm@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/419698 Commit-Ready: Nagendra Modadugu &lt;ngm@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Nagendra Modadugu &lt;ngm@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="419698" owner_email="ngm@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/98/419698/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7096def3b4e4db5918c555482bf93537117851f8" commit="2211ec23a90982781f462ed7cfb3d12345c5220a" commit_message="gooftool: fix verify tpm unittest  On machines with kernel &gt;=3.18, testVerifyTPM fails, since test was designed expecting TPM path from kernel &lt;3.18.  Mox code is is updated to mock a kernel &lt;3.18 system.  Relevant code from VerifyTPM:    tpm_root = '/sys/class/tpm/tpm0/device'   legacy_tpm_root = '/sys/class/misc/tpm0/device'   # TPM device path has been changed in kernel 3.18.   if not os.path.exists(tpm_root):     tpm_root = legacy_tpm_root  BUG=None TEST=Manually on local machine  Change-Id: I7096def3b4e4db5918c555482bf93537117851f8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/420144 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="420144" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/44/420144/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icdeb12b21f0dc3c329f29b206b7b9395ca4c9998" commit="825ae8fa469407751eb2baa6a909ccb4b91f2369" commit_message="i2c_passthru: fix virtual battery operation  In some cases, the virtual battery code creates transactions that violate SB spec.  One example: If the host command is structured as two messages - a write to 0x03 (reg addr), followed by two bytes of write data, the first byte of the second message (write data) will be sent to virtual_battery_read(), as if it were a reg read request.  Let's do the following change for virtual battery: 1. Parse the command more carefully with state machines. 2. Support write caching for some critical registers. 3. Cache more attributes (0x03 and 0x0f).  BUG=chrome-os-partner:59239, chromium:659819 BRANCH=none TEST='power_supply_info' works on kevin  Change-Id: Icdeb12b21f0dc3c329f29b206b7b9395ca4c9998 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/407987 Commit-Ready: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="407987" owner_email="philipchen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/87/407987/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ia0daf4e9944bd7eb0047bafcfde4cb20f4f06933" commit="25dc1495a0912afba4ce98440508912d982ba5d4" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm: dts: rockchip: correct the gpio setting for tiger/fievel BC1.2  The orignal CL:401069 is wrong about BC1.2 function. GPIO should output low not high, and the usb_usb_ilim_sel gpio is GPIO5_B7 not GPIO5_B5.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:58653 TEST=check BC1.2 function, charging current is ~1.5A  Change-Id: Ia0daf4e9944bd7eb0047bafcfde4cb20f4f06933 Signed-off-by: Shunqian Zheng &lt;zhengsq@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/416706 Reviewed-by: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ren Kuo &lt;ren.kuo@quantatw.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="416706" owner_email="zhengsq@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/06/416706/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7dc4865e0c651dfd741657dda6cdbb4950e00a13" commit="24f1725536313c95bd24f09eee313c148a91f80c" commit_message="init: Optimize regulatory domain init time.  regulatory-domain was using &quot;dump_vpd_log&quot; to retrieve all VPD values, which is pretty slow (0.08s per invocation) and should be replaced by the new lightweight vpd_get_value (0.005s).  Also changed the for-loop into a single switch-case so the string comparison is done automatically, and will be more efficient when the constrained regdomain increases.  BUG=chromium:650897 TEST=Restarted and see right regdomain set. CQ-DEPEND=CL:417722  Change-Id: I7dc4865e0c651dfd741657dda6cdbb4950e00a13 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/417644 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="417644" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/44/417644/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><lkgm version="9085.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>